{"name":"Dwarf Fortress","hex":"#1d0200","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dwarf","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any member of a race of beings from (especially Scandinavian and other Germanic) folklore, usually depicted as having some sort of supernatural powers and being skilled in crafting and metalworking, often as short with long beards, and sometimes as clashing with elves.","A person of short stature, often one whose limbs are disproportionately small in relation to the body as compared with typical adults, usually as the result of a genetic condition."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Miniature."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dwarf"},{"term":"fortress","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A fortified place; a large and permanent fortification, sometimes including a town; for example a fort, a castle; a stronghold; a place of defense or security.","A position that, if obtained by the weaker side, will prevent penetration by the opposing side, generally achieving a draw."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To furnish with a fortress or with fortresses; to guard, to fortify."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fortress"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dwarf Fortress","blocks":[{"text":"Dwarf Fortress is a construction and management simulation and roguelike indie video game created by Bay 12 Games. Available as freeware and in development since 2002, its first alpha version was released in 2006 and received attention for being a two-member project surviving solely on donations."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dwarf_Fortress"},{"title":"Fortification","blocks":[{"text":"A fortification is a military construction designed for the defense of territories in warfare, and is used to establish rule in a region during peacetime. The term is derived from Latin fortis (\"strong\") and facere."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Castillo_San_Felipe_del_Morro_%2810_of_1%29.jpg/330px-Castillo_San_Felipe_del_Morro_%2810_of_1%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fortification"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/c6/Dwarf_Fortress_embark_scene.png/330px-Dwarf_Fortress_embark_scene.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/c6/Dwarf_Fortress_embark_scene.png/330px-Dwarf_Fortress_embark_scene.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The game uses text symbols for graphics, unless modified. For example, a dwarf is a colored, bearded smiley-like character and various other letters represent animals. Here, dwarves and livestock can be seen around their wagon of supplies just after embark.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADwarf_Fortress_embark_scene.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/d/d2/Dwarf_Fortress_world_generation.png/330px-Dwarf_Fortress_world_generation.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/d/d2/Dwarf_Fortress_world_generation.png/330px-Dwarf_Fortress_world_generation.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A world being generated and the years being counted. Each game is played in such generated worlds.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADwarf_Fortress_world_generation.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/f/ff/Dwarf_Fortress_adventurer_mode.png/330px-Dwarf_Fortress_adventurer_mode.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/f/ff/Dwarf_Fortress_adventurer_mode.png/330px-Dwarf_Fortress_adventurer_mode.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"C